WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.329
if some part of your politics is genetic

00:00:02.329 --> 00:00:04.759
then the most important decision you

00:00:04.759 --> 00:00:08.209
make in your child's political ideology is

00:00:08.209 --> 00:00:11.059
who you mate with, right? Because

00:00:11.059 --> 00:00:13.219
your genes and their genes join together

00:00:13.219 --> 00:00:16.488
to have children who have particular kinds

00:00:16.488 --> 00:00:19.129
of political biases that are influenced

00:00:19.129 --> 00:00:23.388
by your genetic propensities.

00:00:23.388 --> 00:00:26.509
But how do you know even when

00:00:26.509 --> 00:00:27.799
you ask people maybe they don't know

00:00:27.799 --> 00:00:29.599
maybe they're lying to you. How do

00:00:29.599 --> 00:00:32.358
you actually know in an automatic immediate

00:00:32.358 --> 00:00:34.608
way with somebody else's ideology is?

00:00:34.608 --> 00:00:38.599
And for certain reasons we speculated

00:00:38.599 --> 00:00:40.819
that it had to do with smell. And specifically

00:00:40.819 --> 00:00:44.689
pheromones. This shows you why we thought this.

00:00:44.689 --> 00:00:47.748
So this is a slide where you

00:00:47.748 --> 00:00:50.389
you can see the extent to which

00:00:50.389 --> 00:00:54.889
certain chromosomes are associated.

00:00:54.889 --> 00:00:57.599
And when it's above 3 x 10 to the eighth (power),

00:00:57.659 --> 00:00:59.299
where you see it's significant,

00:00:59.319 --> 00:01:00.759
those are likely to

00:01:00.769 --> 00:01:03.559
occur not just by chance. Right? That it happens

00:01:03.559 --> 00:01:05.809
in a systematic way. And the ones

00:01:05.809 --> 00:01:08.148
that you'll see this is political ideology

00:01:08.148 --> 00:01:09.618
by the way. We're looking at the genes that

00:01:09.618 --> 00:01:11.239
are associated with political ideology.

00:01:11.239 --> 00:01:13.459
This is one of them. And what you'll

00:01:13.459 --> 00:01:16.148
see is that these are the things that are...

00:01:16.148 --> 00:01:18.859
the chromosomes that are associated with this

00:01:18.859 --> 00:01:20.239
are those that are related to smell.

00:01:20.239 --> 00:01:22.699
That are related to olfaction and

00:01:22.699 --> 00:01:26.019
pheromonal strain. So we have these intuitions

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:28.909
based on the genome-wide analyses that

00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:32.118
maybe smell had something to do with the

00:01:32.118 --> 00:01:34.279
way that people were able to

00:01:34.279 --> 00:01:37.249
automatically determine unconsciously

00:01:37.249 --> 00:01:39.019
(this is not a conscious process)

00:01:39.019 --> 00:01:41.328
the political ideology of people that they

00:01:41.328 --> 00:01:43.699
might get involved with. We did

00:01:43.699 --> 00:01:48.279
a study where we looked at facial and body...

00:01:48.279 --> 00:01:51.678
Both sound: we taped people's

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:53.659
voices saying "Hi how are you?"

00:01:53.659 --> 00:01:55.129
We manipulated them so half of them were

00:01:55.129 --> 00:01:57.049
just neutral "Hi how are you?" Half of them

00:01:57.049 --> 00:02:00.218
were more seductive like "Hi how are you?"

00:02:00.218 --> 00:02:04.698
We also took pictures of people. And

00:02:04.698 --> 00:02:06.499
most importantly we did a paradigm based

00:02:06.499 --> 00:02:07.549
on the "wet t-shirt test."

00:02:07.549 --> 00:02:09.109
Although we didn't actually use t-shirts.

00:02:09.109 --> 00:02:13.369
We had people have gauze pads under

00:02:13.369 --> 00:02:14.838
their underarms for a day. And there's

00:02:14.838 --> 00:02:16.489
a particular protocol. They have to

00:02:16.489 --> 00:02:17.939
wash their hair. They have to wash their body.

00:02:17.939 --> 00:02:19.719
They wear it for 24 hours.

00:02:19.719 --> 00:02:21.039
They can exercise, but there are certain

00:02:21.039 --> 00:02:22.479
foods they can't eat. That can't be around

00:02:22.489 --> 00:02:24.999
candles and other things that smell.

00:02:24.999 --> 00:02:26.838
Specifically you can't sleep

00:02:26.838 --> 00:02:28.879
with another person or an animal that night.

00:02:28.879 --> 00:02:30.289
You kind of can't believe people will

00:02:30.289 --> 00:02:36.918
do this for 25 bucks, but they do!

00:02:36.918 --> 00:02:38.448
And they come and...

00:02:38.448 --> 00:02:40.549
they give you the pads the next day.

00:02:40.549 --> 00:02:42.379
And then what you do is you freeze them

00:02:42.379 --> 00:02:44.479
and you slice them up... and you do

00:02:44.479 --> 00:02:46.159
various things. And then you bring in another

00:02:46.159 --> 00:02:47.749
group of people, and you have them smell them.

00:02:47.749 --> 00:02:50.989
And you ask those people, well, what

00:02:50.989 --> 00:02:52.189
does this smell like to you? Is this a

00:02:52.189 --> 00:02:54.079
trustworthy smell? Is this somebody that

00:02:54.079 --> 00:02:55.459
you think is warm? Is it somebody you

00:02:55.459 --> 00:02:56.989
think is competent? Is it somebody...

00:02:56.989 --> 00:02:58.179
blah blah blah

00:02:58.179 --> 00:03:00.439
So what's interesting is there's

00:03:00.439 --> 00:03:02.088
absolutely no correlation on all

00:03:02.088 --> 00:03:04.008
these things like is this person warm, are they

00:03:04.008 --> 00:03:06.769
competent, are they trustworthy...

00:03:06.769 --> 00:03:08.719
there's no correlation. We ask people

00:03:08.719 --> 00:03:11.039
can you tell if this is a liberal or conservative?

00:03:11.039 --> 00:03:12.799
Can't tell at all.

00:03:12.799 --> 00:03:14.478
But you ask them Do you like to smell?

00:03:14.478 --> 00:03:16.219
Are you attracted to this smell? Do you want to

00:03:16.219 --> 00:03:17.899
sleep with this smell? And it

00:03:17.899 --> 00:03:19.739
completely predicts whether or not that

00:03:19.739 --> 00:03:21.979
person's ideology matches their own.

00:03:21.979 --> 00:03:25.219
They can't tell you consciously. But the attraction

00:03:25.219 --> 00:03:28.759
is there. So we had a 190 people.

00:03:28.779 --> 00:03:31.339
We used various pictures. We have

00:03:31.339 --> 00:03:32.808
these voice samples... by the way the

00:03:32.808 --> 00:03:35.689
voice stuff was interesting. We didn't get

00:03:35.689 --> 00:03:37.788
any findings by whether or not the voices

00:03:37.788 --> 00:03:39.619
were seductive or neutral. But what

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:42.228
we did get are asymmetries by conservatives

00:03:42.228 --> 00:03:43.619
and liberals. So liberals

00:03:43.619 --> 00:03:45.519
really don't like the sound of conservative voices.

00:03:45.519 --> 00:03:48.439
And conservatives really don't like

00:03:48.439 --> 00:03:50.819
the smell of liberals.

00:03:50.819 --> 00:03:54.859
And this is the slide that shows this.

00:03:54.899 --> 00:03:58.519
This is conservatives smelling conservatives.

00:03:58.519 --> 00:03:59.599
Liberals smelling liberals.

00:03:59.619 --> 00:04:01.419
The M and F have to do with males

00:04:01.429 --> 00:04:04.579
and female. And it's a

00:04:04.579 --> 00:04:06.139
little backwards right so this one is

00:04:06.139 --> 00:04:07.729
males smelling females, males smelling males,

00:04:07.729 --> 00:04:09.859
females smelling... so the people who like

00:04:09.859 --> 00:04:11.479
each other smell the least are...

00:04:11.479 --> 00:04:13.279
Women like each other smells the least.

00:04:13.279 --> 00:04:16.859
This was a heterosexual sample I should say.

00:04:16.869 --> 00:04:18.919
So you can see that there's

00:04:18.919 --> 00:04:20.299
there's differences. And there are

00:04:20.299 --> 00:04:22.369
asymmetries. But these are

00:04:22.369 --> 00:04:24.259
all statistically significant differences

00:04:24.259 --> 00:04:28.219
where you can see that these are related

00:04:28.219 --> 00:04:31.399
to people's automatic, you know,

00:04:31.399 --> 00:04:34.309
unconscious inferences about how

00:04:34.309 --> 00:04:36.829
these things work. This study was very

00:04:36.829 --> 00:04:38.479
interesting when I did it. Because the

00:04:38.479 --> 00:04:40.309
first day I was really not sure it

00:04:40.309 --> 00:04:41.719
was going to work. And we opened up the

00:04:41.719 --> 00:04:44.499
vial. And I gave it to my lab manager.

00:04:44.499 --> 00:04:46.519
And she smelled it. And she's like, yeah, it's okay.

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:47.399
Because we were kind of like,

00:04:47.399 --> 00:04:50.019
is this going to gross people out?

00:04:50.019 --> 00:04:52.379
She brought in her boyfriend and said: smell this.

00:04:52.379 --> 00:04:55.379
And he smelled it and he threw up.

00:04:55.379 --> 00:04:57.439
Like I had to do this Vegas thing on him

00:04:57.439 --> 00:04:58.669
to stop him from throwing up. And he's like

00:04:58.669 --> 00:05:01.189
"That is rancid!" And I smelled it.

00:05:01.189 --> 00:05:02.629
I'm like, it's not rancid. She smelled it and said

00:05:02.629 --> 00:05:04.609
it's not rancid. And I was like

00:05:04.609 --> 00:05:07.779
this study is so going to work.

00:05:16.499 --> 00:05:18.559
 

